From 3dd51294fb88f32873c94dd4eea58f60fd525e4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:40:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip: apu-expert-gtt P1.1 + P2 -- a registered GTT expert
 store sized by -lme

A UMA-only resident expert tier: ONE anonymous region (mmap + MADV_HUGEPAGE, registered
ONE cudaHostRegister(Mapped|ReadOnly)) that the hottest MoE expert tables are placed in and
that MUL_MAT_ID reads in place, with no host pool, no arena and no slab below it.

- the store's region + bump allocator + census live in ggml/src/ggml-cuda/gtt-expert-store.{cu,cuh};
  the buffer type is in ggml-cuda.cu, following the KV-region pattern (a DEVICE buft with the plain
  device type's vtable contract and a per-device unique name), and two device hooks let the model
  loader open it and print its census.
- -lme sizes it (P1.1): N GiB exactly, or auto = MOE_HOST_LIMIT_FRAC of MemAvailable, capped at the
  set; the SAME budget and the SAME heat ranking as the discrete arm, decided before any tensor is
  placed.  It engages without -ncmoe, and common/arg.cpp gains the UMA branch of the help text.
- the fill is the buffered pread arm, straight from the GGUF into the slot (no alignment round-out).
- MOE_EXPERT_GTT=0 (kill switch) reproduces today's behaviour byte for byte; MOE_EXPERT_GTT_RO=0
  registers the region writable, which is the A/B that proves the read-rate claim on this region.
- ALL-RESIDENT arm only: no eviction (P3), no streaming/pipelined fill (P4), no prefill streaming
  (P5).  Whatever did not fit the budget keeps its layer's device buffer, and the census says so.

Verified on halo (gfx1151, 123 GiB, ROCm 10.1.0): same-seed greedy text identical on 35B-A3B and
Flash-Next for store-off / store-auto / -lme 6; -lme 6 realises exactly 6144.0 MiB; auto on a
fitting set is the whole set (123 or 144 tables) with zero evictions; 100 % huge pages; pp512
within noise of the plain device buffer with the registered READ-ONLY arm (-0.4 / -1.25 %) and
-5.9 / -6.2 % with it registered writable; check-gpu-faults.sh clean.
